62:- `.pi/extensions/goal/queue-tools.ts` already provides `start_queued_goal` for atomic direct handoff and `dequeue_goal` for manual consumption after separate successful handling.
77:- Tell the agent to semantically interpret prose/JIT orchestration using current context rather than relying on code parser heuristics.
79:- Explicitly allow one orchestration queue item to require as many consecutive active goals as needed before the agent calls `dequeue_goal`.
80:- Tell the agent to call `dequeue_goal` only after the orchestration item is satisfied.
91:- [ ] Update `.pi/extensions/goal/queue-steering.ts` so `queueSteeringContent()` always explains the two queue-head modes: direct queued goal vs prose/JIT orchestration.
94:- [ ] Add explicit prose/JIT guidance: use current context, create/start/enqueue concrete goal(s) with existing tools, and do not parse prose in extension code.
96:- [ ] Add explicit safe-consumption guidance: call `dequeue_goal` only after the orchestration item is satisfied; leave it queued when blocked/uncertain.
103:- Non-template queue steering content tells the agent the objective may be direct or prose/JIT orchestration.
108:- Prose/JIT orchestration guidance explicitly says to call `dequeue_goal` only after the orchestration item is satisfied, and to leave it queued when blocked or uncertain.
116:Primary invariant: queued-goal steering must help the agent choose the correct handoff mode for the queue head. Direct queued goals should use `start_queued_goal`; prose/JIT orchestration should be interpreted from current context and remain queued until fully satisfied.
